#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This Procedure demonstrates a Split-Mu braking test, with Open-Loop controls being used for both the throttle and brakes.
#
#The vehicle starts from an initial speed of 65 kph but with the throttle closed. The master cylinder brake pressure is set to 15 MPa at 0.3 seconds. Since this test is taking place on a split-mu surface (See the road dataset "Split Mu"), it can be used to evaluate the split-mu capabilities of an ABS system, or to investigate what happens when a vehicle not equipped with ABS attempts to stop on a split-mu surface.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

